svdint4 includes an Apache-2.0 derived minimal binding around the Nunchaku
W4A4/SVDQuant CUDA kernel path.

The package exposes INT4 GEMM, activation quantization, SVD correction, packed
Turing W4A8, and a bundled Turing SageAttention2 path. Model wrappers, RoPE
fusion, W8A8, AWQ, NVFP4, cache logic, and pipeline integrations are
intentionally omitted.

The staged Turing ConvRot quantizer and segmented RMSNorm+AdaLN kernel under
`csrc/turing/` are derived from comfy-kitchen's Apache-2.0 CUDA implementation:

  https://github.com/Comfy-Org/comfy-kitchen

The CUDA kernel subset under csrc/svdint4 is derived from Nunchaku:

  https://github.com/nunchaku-ai/nunchaku

Nunchaku is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the
original license text is kept in LICENSES/nunchaku-LICENCE.txt.

The derived subset has been reduced to the files required for INT4 GEMM,
activation quantization, and SVD correction dispatch. The package build no
longer depends on a sibling nunchaku checkout.

The SM75 attention sources are derived from wjie98's Apache-2.0 SageAttention
branch `feature/turing-sm75-backend`, commit
`abc695cb9ed9572deb83fd9bb85f0fb815347ebd`, itself derived from SageAttention:

  https://github.com/wjie98/SageAttention/tree/feature/turing-sm75-backend
  https://github.com/thu-ml/SageAttention

The vendored CUDA and Python support is kept under `csrc/turing/sage2` and
`svdint4/turing_sage2`. SageAttention is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0; its license text is in LICENSES/sageattention-LICENSE.txt.
